      "warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains 5 core rules: warehousing classification and ordering process, warehousing verification requirements, placement requirements, system data processing requirements, and prohibition of virtual warehousing orders.",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc is clearly divided into daily stocking procurement and order stocking, and describes the correct ordering process respectively?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc clearly stipulates that the products received on the same day need to complete the system data processing on the same day?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains outbound voucher requirements, information verification rules, a total of 3 core rules for prohibiting dummy outbound orders, and the complete shipping process for direct stores?",
      "warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc Whether the 8 steps are complete, that is, the shipper receives the order→ View→ the inventory check information Classify the picking list→ according to the inventory area Dispatch the→ picking to the picking person Package the return order→ Shipper Accept the order Generate→ the delivery order Shipper dispatch Delivery→ person Check the delivery person Delivery customer sign?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains inventory estimation requirements, backlog handling rules, storage requirements, inventory and accountability requirements A total of 4 core rules?",
      "warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc Whether it is clear that more than 3 months must be reported in time, and more than half a year must be requested from the general manager of the marketing headquarters?",
      "Whether the warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains three inventory cycles: daily inventory, monthly inventory, and mid-year/year-end comprehensive inventory, and it is clear that signature confirmation is required for the initial inventory review?",
      "warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains 5 core rules: personnel access requirements, cargo storage requirements, fire management requirements, \"three defenses\" work requirements, personnel handover and confidentiality requirements",
      "Does warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc clearly stipulate that smoking and open flames are strictly prohibited in the warehouse, and that evacuation routes and safe exits are unimpeded?",
      "Whether the \"three defenses\" work requirements are clearly fireproof, moisture-proof, anti-theft three work?",
      "Whether it is clear in warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc that warehouse personnel must be checked one by one before transferring or leaving, and the transfer to both parties and the department head must sign and confirm?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc is classified and arranged according to the business process order of \"Inbound Management - Inventory Control - Outbound Management - Daily Operation and Maintenance\"?",
      "Whether it is clearly stated in warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc that the warehousing specification is the basis for inventory control, and that inventory control is the prerequisite for outbound compliance Business closed-loop logic?",
      "Does warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc clearly state the complementary relationship between inventory management specification quantity and inventory, warehouse daily management specification storage and safety?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc is listed separately as a \"Common Red Line Rule\" module and contains two common guidelines: \"Requirements for Consistent Checking of Accounts\" and \"Prohibition of Falsely Opening No Physical Documents\"?",
      "Whether the warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc contains both a prohibition of dummy inbound orders and a prohibition of dummy outbound orders?",
      "Whether the \"first in, first out\" principle is separately described in warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc Two specific application scenarios in the daily storage and delivery links?",
      "Whether warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc requires placement according to schedule to facilitate first-in, first-out, and whether it is explicitly required to avoid stagnant backlogs and expired depreciation in the outbound.?",
      "warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc Whether the content completely overwrites all the core rules required for extraction in the original four files, no omissions?",
      "Whether the warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc structure is divided into six main modules, namely warehousing management, inventory control, outbound management, daily operation and maintenance, general red line rules, business logic description?",
      "Whether it is clearly stipulated in warehouse_core_operation_standard_manual.doc that when there is a discrepancy in the account, the reason must be traced, the responsibility must be clarified, and the process must be escalated.?"
