    "rubrics": [
      "Does the post_summary.xlsx file contain a total of 100 data records, corresponding to the processing of all 100 JSON files?",
      "Is the data in post_summary.xlsx correctly sorted by post_id from small to large, post_1 on the first line and post_100 on the last line?",
      "Does post_summary.xlsx contain 20 data columns covering all key fields extracted from JSON?",
      "Does the table contain post_id, platform, content_type, caption, hashtags, post_date, scheduled, status, campaign_id as basic information columns?",
      "Does the table include engagement_likes, engagement_comments, engagement_shares, engagement_saves, engagement_engagement_rate interaction indicator columns?",
      "Does the table contain columns for audience_reach, audience_impressions, audience_followers_gained, audience_click_through_rate audience insights?",
      "Does the table contain media_image_url, media_video_url columns?",
      "Can files with JSON syntax errors (such as line wrapping in the content_type field) be successfully parsed without losing content?",
      "All json files are processed correctly and none of the post records are missing in post_summary.xlsx?",
      "does the platform column convert arrays to comma-separated strings, such as [\"instagram\"] to \"instagram\"?",
      "does the hashtags column convert all tag arrays to comma-separated strings, preserving all tag information?",
      "Is the campaign_id of the first record (post_1) in post_summary.xlsx camp_2 and engagement_engagement_rate \"3.51 %\"?",
      "Is the campaign_id of post_92 in post_summary.xlsx camp_13 and engagement_engagement_rate \"5.99 %\"?",
      "Is the campaign_id of post_93 in post_summary.xlsx camp_14, and the content_type corrected to \"video image\"?",
      "Is the engagement_likes value of post_100 correctly read and saved in the engagement_likes column of the corresponding row?",
      "Are all value types (likes, comments, shares, saves, reach, impressions, followers_gained) saved numerically and able to participate in the calculation?",
      "Are all percent type data (engagement_rate, click_through_rate) in the same percentage string format?",
      "Is the Boolean scheduled field correctly converted to the true/false text value in the table?",
      "Does the table have a one-line, one-post structure, with data for only one social media post per row?",
      "The output table has a clear structure and each key field has a unique column, which is convenient for screening and analyzing the delivery effect?"
    ],
