      "Does the output file `social-media-post-plan.md` include a section summarizing historical data analysis?",
      "Does the data-analysis section correctly state that there are 100 historical posts in total?",
      "Does the data-analysis section correctly state that Instagram has 80 posts with an average engagement rate of 5.38%?",
      "Does the data-analysis section correctly state that Facebook has 20 posts with an average engagement rate of 6.19%?",
      "Does the data-analysis section correctly state that the pure-text content type has the highest average engagement rate at 5.97%?",
      "Does the data-analysis section correctly state that the video-plus-image content type has the lowest average engagement rate at 4.74%?",
      "Does the plan clearly state that the total planned number of posts for next month is 96?",
      "Is the platform allocation in the plan 32 Facebook posts, accounting for 33.3%, and 64 Instagram posts, accounting for 66.7%?",
      "Is the content-type allocation in the plan 36 pure-text posts, accounting for 37.5%, 35 image posts, accounting for 36.5%, and 25 video-plus-image posts, accounting for 26%?",
      "Does the plan include a complete weekly publishing schedule table that clearly distinguishes posting times for weekdays and weekends?",
      "Does the plan include a detailed content schedule covering four weeks plus one additional week, for a total of five weeks?",
      "Does the week-one schedule include monthly goals and new-product teaser content for Instagram and Facebook on March 1?",
      "Does week two include a Women's Day campaign schedule, including the March 8 Women's Day campaign launch content?",
      "Does week three include a quality-focused campaign schedule, including the Consumer Rights Day quality-commitment content on March 15?",
      "Does week four include a new-product launch campaign schedule, including the formal product launch content on March 24?",
      "Does week five include a monthly recap schedule covering summary content from March 29 to March 31?",
      "Does the plan include a complete hashtag strategy divided into three categories: fixed brand hashtags, general industry hashtags, and thematic campaign hashtags?",
      "Do the fixed brand hashtags include `#product`, `#innovation`, `#marketing`, and `#socialmedia`?",
      "Does the plan clearly set the overall average engagement-rate target within the range of 5.8% to 6.2%?",
      "Does the plan clearly set the target for new followers at more than 140 million?",
      "Does the plan include a performance-tracking and adjustment mechanism covering four levels: daily monitoring, weekly summary, monthly review, and flexible adjustment?",
      "Does the output file provide a reasonable explanation for adjusting the posting ratio based on the historical data-analysis results?",
      "Does the output file clearly state that the date range is from March 1, 2024 to March 31, 2024?",
      "Does the output file mention the three core elements of content type, posting time, and publishing platform?",
      "Based on comparison of the historical data, does it conclude that Facebook performs better than Instagram in engagement and adjust the posting ratio accordingly?"
