    "task": "Based on the papers on AI and aerospace systems on the desktop, write \"A Review of the Application of Formal Methods in AI Generation and Aerospace Systems\"\n\nTask background: As a cross-domain researcher, you need to explore the application of formal methods (such as LTLf synthesis) and generative models (such as 3D generation) in key fields such as aerospace. You have three papers on hand: Multi-Property Synthesis (Multi-Property Synthesis), Editable 3D Generation (Proc3D), and Aerospace Power System Health Management (SpaceHMchat). You need to read these papers, understand how they use AI technology to solve complex problems, and explore the intersection potential of formal methods and generative models.\n\nTask goal: Please complete a review report (PDF format) based on the three PDF papers in the data/input/ directory. Specific requirements:\n\nWrite an abstract for each paper, including research questions, methods, and main findings.\n\nAnalyze the significance of the multi-attribute synthesis method in AI planning, how Proc3D's PCG representation promotes editable 3D generation, and how SpaceHMchat realizes human-machine collaborative health management.\n\nThe potential application of these methods in safety-critical systems such as aerospace is discussed.\n\nAppropriately cite the paper content in the review and add hyperlinks to relevant parts of the original text.\n\nThe output file is saved as output/formal_methods_and_generation_applications_survey.pdf.",
